<SubpageLayout title="Naoero ebõk · Culture & Heritage" description="Food, family, church, language and the symbols that carry Nauruan identity." sectionEmoji="🎭" sectionLabel="Ebõk i en" includeFooter={true} locale="na">
  <p>Nauruan culture is shaped by island life: family, church, fishing, local gatherings and a history that is carried through language and stories. Heritage matters because it keeps the country connected to the land and sea around it.</p>
<h2>Culture in practice</h2>
<p>Tradition is visible in community events, ceremony, food and the way people support one another. The island's small size makes cultural continuity very visible.</p>
<div class="info-box"><h4>🪶 Identity markers</h4><p>Flag, coat of arms, anthem, church life and tribal memory are all part of how Nauru understands itself.</p></div>
